{"name":"Stadium Lawn","hex":"#9af764","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stadium","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A venue where sporting events are held.","An Ancient Greek racecourse, especially, the Olympic course for foot races."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stadium"},{"term":"lawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ground (generally in front of or around a house) covered with grass kept closely mown.","An open space between woods."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To furnish with a lawn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stadium","blocks":[{"text":"A stadium is a place or venue for (mostly) outdoor sports, concerts, or other events and consists of a field or stage completely or partially surrounded by a tiered structure designed to allow spectators to stand or sit and view the event. Pausanias noted that for about half a century the only event at the ancient Greek Olympic festival was the race that comprised one length of the stadion at Olympia, where the word \"stadium\" originated. Most of the stadiums with a capacity of at least 10,000 are used for association football. Other popular stadium sports include gridiron football, baseball, cricket, the various codes of rugby, field lacrosse, bandy, and bullfighting. Many large sports venues are also used for concerts. Many modern designs are increasingly incorporating sustainability features such as energy efficiency and proper waste management systems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Narendra_Modi_Stadium_view_from_the_gallery.jpg/330px-Narendra_Modi_Stadium_view_from_the_gallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stadium","wikidata":"Q483110"},{"title":"Lawn","blocks":[{"text":"A lawn is an area of soil-covered land planted with grasses and other durable plants such as clover which is maintained at a short height with a lawn mower and used for aesthetic and recreational purposes. It is also commonly referred to as part of a garden."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/The_Lawn_UVa_2007.jpg/330px-The_Lawn_UVa_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawn","wikidata":"Q207766"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Ancient_Olympia_Stadium_in_Greece_%2851224128585%29.jpg/500px-Ancient_Olympia_Stadium_in_Greece_%2851224128585%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Ancient_Olympia_Stadium_in_Greece_%2851224128585%29.jpg/1280px-Ancient_Olympia_Stadium_in_Greece_%2851224128585%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Ancient_Olympia_Stadium_in_Greece_%2851224128585%29.jpg/500px-Ancient_Olympia_Stadium_in_Greece_%2851224128585%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stadium at Olympia were built ~776 BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAncient_Olympia_Stadium_in_Greece_(51224128585).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Circus_Maximus%2C_plan_de_Rome_de_Paul_Bigot%2C_universit%C3%A9_de_Caen_MRSH.JPG/500px-Circus_Maximus%2C_plan_de_Rome_de_Paul_Bigot%2C_universit%C3%A9_de_Caen_MRSH.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Circus_Maximus%2C_plan_de_Rome_de_Paul_Bigot%2C_universit%C3%A9_de_Caen_MRSH.JPG/1280px-Circus_Maximus%2C_plan_de_Rome_de_Paul_Bigot%2C_universit%C3%A9_de_Caen_MRSH.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Circus_